"Parameters: - model (nn.Module): The PyTorch model to be modified. - "
"regex_patterns (list of str): List of regex patterns to match layer names"
" to keep unfrozen. Note that you cannot use a dot as a wildcard character"
" in the patterns since it is reserved for separating layer names. Also, "
"to match the entire layer name, the pattern should start with “^” and end"
" with “\\(\", otherwise it will match any part of the layer name. The "
"range pattern part is optional and it is not compiled as a regex pattern "
"which means you must put \"\\)” before the range pattern if you want to "
"match the entire layer name. E.g., "
"[“^model.embed_tokens.weight\\([:32000]\", "
"\"layers.2[0-9]+.block_sparse_moe.gate.[a-z]+\\)”]"
msgstr ""

